        "original_id": "ddbf2d8f-1540-50c9-912f-c9c7044e6ff8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Der Freischütz, Il trovatore, Magic Hunter\n- People: Carl Maria von Weber, Friedrich Kind, Giuseppe Verdi, Salvadore Cammarano, Antonio García Gutiérrez, Ildikó Enyedi\n- Concepts: opera, libretto, fantasy film\n\nFacts:\n- In 1836, Antonio García Gutiérrez wrote the play \"El trovador,\" which became the basis for Il trovatore.\n- Der Freischütz, Op. 77, J. 277, is a German opera with spoken dialogue in three acts by Carl Maria von Weber and a libretto by Friedrich Kind.\n- Der Freischütz is usually translated as \"The Marksman\" or \"The Freeshooter.\"\n- Il trovatore is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi with an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano.\n- Il trovatore means \"The Troubadour\" in Italian.\n- In 1994, Ildikó Enyedi wrote and directed Magic Hunter, a Hungarian-Swiss-French fantasy film.\n- Magic Hunter is loosely inspired by the opera Der Freischütz.\n- Magic Hunter is titled \"Bűvös vadász\" in Hungarian and \"Freischütz\" in French.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d20aad0c-885d-5357-8570-d7de136e0fed",
        "text": "Page: Der Freischütz. Sentence: Der Freischütz , Op. 77, J. 277, (usually translated as \"The Marksman\" or \"The Freeshooter\") is a German opera with spoken dialogue in three acts by Carl Maria von Weber with a libretto by Friedrich Kind.\nPage: Il trovatore. Sentence: Il trovatore (] ; Italian for \"The Troubadour\") is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi to an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano, based on the play \"El trovador\" (1836) by Antonio García Gutiérrez.\nPage: Magic Hunter. Sentence: Magic Hunter (Hungarian: \"Bűvös vadász\" , French: \"Freischütz\" ) is a 1994 Hungarian-Swiss-French fantasy film written and directed by Ildikó Enyedi and loosely inspired to the opera Der Freischütz.",
